-- title:
--   Universal H⁰ equals the base for the X₁(Mp) two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, containing a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L$ inside the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) attached to $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be an element, nonzero as a registered fact, whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}(q)$ of the $j$-invariant. Write $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the map from the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebras `chartAlgFin A K j` and `chartAlgInf A K j` of $K$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Then for every commutative ring $B$ with an $A$-algebra structure, equipping $\Gamma(X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} B, \top)$ with the $B$-algebra structure induced by the second projection via `Scheme.TwoAffineOpenCover.algebraOfHom`, the structure map $B \to \Gamma(X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} B, \top)$ is bijective.
--
--   This is the statement that $H^0$ of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the valuation ring $A$ of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ is the base ring, universally in $A$-algebras $B$ — the cohomological input needed to view the model as a relative curve with trivial relative $H^0$. It feeds the construction of the relative Picard data for this model in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
